{"collection_no":"146654","record_type":"col","lng":5.400588,"lat":47.907429,"collection_name":"Lac de Charmes section 2a, bed 20","n_occs":1,"early_interval":"Spinatum","max_ma":192.9,"min_ma":184.2,"reference_no":"47417","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"stated in text","latlng_precision":"6","geogscale":"small collection","geogcomments":"On the southern side of the “Lac de Charmes”, near the road D74. The outcrop is interrupted by a large tree whose roots have prevented vegetation growth at that point, revealing layers of the succession beneath. The two parts of the second outcrop are separated by a fault, so are described in two lithologic sections (2a and 2b).","environment":"carbonate indet.","primary_reference":"J. Bardin, I. Rouget, and F. Cecca. 2013. Late Pliensbachian (Early Jurassic) ammonites from Lac de Charmes (Haute-Marne, France): systematic, biostratigraphy and palaeobiogeography. Geodiversitas 35:309-334"},
