{"collection_no":"161187","record_type":"col","lng":5.775600,"lat":45.990601,"collection_name":"River Dorches, northwest of Orbagnoux mine","n_occs":1,"early_interval":"Late Kimmeridgian","max_ma":152.21,"min_ma":149.2,"reference_no":"52512","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"stated in text","latlng_precision":"4","altitude_value":"597","altitude_unit":"meters","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"The fossils were collected in the small valley of the river Dorches (a river Rhône tributary), situated on the territory of the Corbonod village, northwest of Orbagnoux mine (Long. 5 46' 32.2\"E, Lat. 45 59' 26.3\"N, alt. 597 m). The highly bituminous black shales inside of the Orbagnoux mine (Chateauneuf et al., 1982) contain few macrofossils (A Nel, pers. obs., 2012): mainly rather poorly preserved ammonites and bivalves, foraminifers and ostracods. On the contrary, fossil plants, fishes and crustaceans are known in other layers outside of the mine.","environment":"lagoonal/restricted shallow subtidal","primary_reference":"A. Nel, P. Nel, and R. Krieg-Jacquier, J. M. Pouillon, R. Garrouste. 2014. Exceptionally preserved insect fossils in the Late Jurassic lagoon of Orbagnoux (Rhône Valley, France). PeerJ 2(e510):1-16"},
