{"collection_no":"174767","record_type":"col","lng":5.559500,"lat":44.541500,"collection_name":"Le Chouet, bed 79","n_occs":4,"early_interval":"Late Tithonian","max_ma":145.06,"min_ma":143.1,"reference_no":"57139","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"estimated from map","latlng_precision":"4","geogscale":"small collection","geogcomments":"The locality lies in the cliffed upper valley of the River Drôme, in pine forest (Long 5°33'33\"E, Lat 44°32'32\"N) off the local road (D306) from Die to Valdrôme. It comprises a low mural section, 200 m-long, along a single track road on the north-west side of a precipitous gorge, the Ravin de Fournet. The section extends around the slope from an altitude of 928 m to a little above 1000 m.","environment":"carbonate indet.","primary_reference":"L. G. Bulot, C. Frau, and W. A. P. Wimbledon. 2014. New and poorly known Perisphinctoidea (Ammonitina) from the Upper Tithonian of Le Chouet (Drôme, SE France). Volumina Jurassica 12:113-128"},
