{"collection_no":"183702","record_type":"col","lng":5.520000,"lat":44.547001,"collection_name":"Charens, bed 17","n_occs":2,"early_interval":"Middle Tithonian","max_ma":149.2,"min_ma":143.1,"reference_no":"61367","cc":"FR","latlng_basis":"estimated from map","latlng_precision":"3","geogscale":"outcrop","geogcomments":"The Charens section is located about three kilometres to the west of Le Chouet (Drôme, France). The locality lies in the upper valley of the Drôme River (Long 5°31'08\"E, Lat 44°32'42\"N) off the local road (D93) from Die to Beaurières. It comprises a low mural section, 250 m-long, along a single-track road (D145) on the east side of the Charens gorge. The section extends around the slope from an altitude of 756 m to 768 m and dips 10 degrees to the North.","environment":"carbonate indet.","primary_reference":"C. Frau, L. G. Bulot, and W. A. P. Wimbledon, C. Ifrim. 2016. Upper Tithonian ammonites (Himalayitidae Spath, 1925 and Neocomitidae Salfeld, 1921) from Charens (Drôme, France). Geologica Carpathica 67:543-559"},
