{"collection_no":"280041","record_type":"col","lng":6.595042,"lat":43.976791,"collection_name":"Synclinal d'Allons, La Tuilière","n_occs":7,"early_interval":"Priabonian","max_ma":37.71,"min_ma":33.9,"reference_no":"76944","cc":"FR","state":"Provence-Alpes-Cote d'Azur","county":"Alpes-de-Haute-Provence","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"6","geogcomments":"Topographic map 1/25,000, 3541 W, Saint-André-des-Alpes,\nx = 939.775, y = 3197.550. \nBadlands in the east flank of the Ivoire valley, exposing gray\nsilty marls.\n• Sample (about 200 kg) from + 2 until + 4 m of the section;\n• Sample (about 30 kg) from + 10 until + 12 m of the section","environment":"terrestrial indet.","primary_reference":"A. Girone and D. Nolf. 2009. Fish otoliths from the Priabonian (Late Eocene) of North Italy and South-East France – Their paleobiogeographical significance. Revue de micropaléontologie 52:195-218"},
{"collection_no":"280042","record_type":"col","lng":6.520331,"lat":43.959690,"collection_name":"Synclinal d'Allons, site B: banks of the torrent Ivoire","n_occs":24,"early_interval":"Priabonian","max_ma":37.71,"min_ma":33.9,"reference_no":"76944","cc":"FR","state":"Provence-Alpes-Cote d'Azur","county":"Alpes-de-Haute-Provence","latlng_basis":"based on nearby landmark","latlng_precision":"6","geogcomments":"Topographic map 1/25,000, 3541 W, Saint-André-des-Alpes,\nx = 939.950, y = 3196.750.\nGray silty marls with nummulites (sample of about 300 kg),\nexposed in the banks of the river l’Ivoire, about 125 m SE of “La\nBastide neuve”. The upper course of the Ivoire is called “Torrent\ndes Garets”, which is the name that Boussac (1912) used instead\nof l’Ivoire, that appears on the latest 1/25,000 topographic map.","environment":"terrestrial indet.","primary_reference":"A. Girone and D. Nolf. 2009. Fish otoliths from the Priabonian (Late Eocene) of North Italy and South-East France – Their paleobiogeographical significance. Revue de micropaléontologie 52:195-218"},
